  "text": "Now let me check each rule against the settings.json file:\n\n## Rule Compliance Check\n\n**R1: limits.maxUploadMb must not exceed 50.**\n- Value in settings.json: `18`\n- Status: ✅ **MET** (18 ≤ 50)\n\n**R2: auth.sessionTtlMinutes must be between 5 and 120 inclusive.**\n- Value in settings.json: `17`\n- Status: ✅ **MET** (5 ≤ 17 ≤ 120)\n\n**R3: features.beta must be false.**\n- Value in settings.json: `true`\n- Status: ❌ **NOT MET** (true ≠ false)\n\n**R4: smtp.host must end with \".example.com\".**\n- Value in settings.json: `\"smtp.example.com\"`\n- Status: ✅ **MET** (ends with \".example.com\")\n\n**R5: retention.days must be at least 30.**\n- Value in settings.json: `53`\n- Status: ✅ **MET** (53 ≥ 30)\n\n## Conclusion\n\n**settings.json is NOT COMPLIANT**\n\nThe configuration fails to meet **Rule R3** because `features.beta` is set to `true` when it must be `false`. All other 4 rules are satisfied. To achieve full compliance, `features.beta` must be changed from `true` to `false`."
